---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Pakistan Property Tax Guide: Capital Gains Tax & Calculator";
const description = "Complete Pakistan property tax guide. Learn provincial property tax rates, capital gains tax on property sales, token charges, and calculate property tax in Pakistan.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551288049-bebda4e38f71?w=1200&q=80";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/pakistan-property-tax-guide";
const author = "Usman Tariq";
const authorBio = "Real estate tax specialist covering property taxation across all Pakistani provinces.";
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
const readTime = "10 min read";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is provincial property tax (UIPT) calculated in Pakistan?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Annual property tax is a provincial levy charged on the Annual Rental Value (ARV) or gross rental value of urban properties. Rates vary by province (e.g. 5% of ARV in Punjab, category rates in Sindh/KPK)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the Capital Gains Tax (CGT) rate on property sales in Pakistan?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CGT applies to profits from property sales. For properties acquired on or after July 1, 2024, FBR active taxpayer filers pay a flat 15% CGT, while non-filers face higher rates up to 45%."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between buyer and seller withholding tax under Section 236C and 236K?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Section 236C is advance withholding tax paid by the seller at property transfer, while Section 236K is advance tax paid by the buyer. Filers pay significantly lower rates than non-filers on both."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} canonical={canonical} author={author} authorBio={authorBio} lastUpdated={lastUpdated} readTime={readTime}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-sm">
          <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Home</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/blogs" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Blogs</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary" aria-current="page">Pakistan Property Tax Guide</span></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Pakistan Property Tax Guide: Capital Gains Tax & Calculator</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: August 2026 | Verified FBR & Provincial Rules | 10 min read</p>

          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1525625293386-3f8f99389edd?w=1200&q=80" alt="Urban property development in Pakistan" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />

          <!-- Early Calculator CTA -->
          <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 dark:border-primary/20 dark:bg-primary/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Calculate Pakistan Property Tax & CGT</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1">Estimate capital gains tax (15%), buyer/seller withholding (236C & 236K), and provincial property taxes.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/countries/pakistan/property-tax/property-tax-calculator" class="btn btn-primary text-sm font-semibold shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5">
              Launch Pakistan Property Tax Calculator →
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>Property ownership in Pakistan involves several layers of taxation, including annual provincial property taxes (UIPT) and federal advance withholding taxes under <strong>Sections 236C and 236K</strong> of the <em>Income Tax Ordinance, 2001</em>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Provincial Property Tax (UIPT)</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Annual Property Tax (UIPT):</strong> Provincial tax based on ARV or DC value.</li>
              <li><strong>Capital Gains Tax:</strong> On the profit from sale, calculated as sale price minus purchase price.</li>
              <li><strong>Withholding Tax (236C/236K):</strong> Advance taxes deducted at the time of sale and purchase.</li>
              <li><strong>Stamp Duty and Registration Fees:</strong> Provincial charges for deed registration.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>To simplify this process, use our <a href="/countries/pakistan/property-tax/property-tax-calculator">Pakistan property tax calculator</a>, which estimates UIPT, CGT, stamp duty, and withholding tax for all provinces.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Property taxation in Pakistan involves a mix of federal and provincial obligations. Annual UIPT keeps property owners in the provincial tax net, while capital gains tax and withholding tax apply at the point of transaction. Being a registered filer dramatically reduces your CGT and withholding tax burden. For accurate estimates of all property-related taxes, use our <a href="/countries/pakistan/property-tax/property-tax-calculator">Pakistan property tax calculator</a> or read our <a href="/blogs/pakistan-capital-gain-tax-guide">Pakistan capital gain tax guide</a> for more details on CGT.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the property tax rate in Punjab?</h3>
            <p>Punjab charges Urban Immovable Property Tax at 5% of the Annual Rental Value under the Punjab UIPT Act 1958. The province is moving toward a capital-value model based on DC rates.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the capital gains tax rate on property in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>For properties acquired on or after July 1, 2024, CGT is a flat 15% for ATL filers on all holding periods. For earlier acquisitions, CGT ranges from 15% (short-term) to 0% (held more than 6 years) for filers.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How do I pay property tax online in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>You can pay property tax online through provincial portals: ePay Punjab (epay.punjab.gov.pk) for Punjab, ePay Sindh (epay.gos.pk) for Sindh, and the respective excise portals for KPK and Islamabad.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the difference between property tax and stamp duty?</h3>
            <p>Property tax (UIPT) is an annual tax for owning land. Stamp duty is a one-time provincial tax paid at the Sub-Registrar office when a property deed is registered.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do non-filers pay more property tax than filers?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Non-filers pay higher withholding taxes on property transactions. For Section 236C, non-filers may pay 3% to 5% or more than filers. On CGT, non-filers pay three times the filer rate for older properties.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the early payment rebate for property tax?</h3>
            <p>Punjab and Islamabad offer approximately a 5% rebate when the full year's property tax is paid on or before September 30. Check your provincial excise department for the exact deadline and rebate percentage.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How is capital gains tax calculated on property sales?</h3>
            <p>CGT is calculated on the net capital gain: sale price (or FBR valuation, whichever is higher) minus purchase price, minus allowable improvement costs and brokerage. The result is multiplied by the applicable CGT rate based on holding period and filer status.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Related Calculators</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
              <a href="/countries/pakistan/property-tax/property-tax-calculator" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">Pakistan Property Tax Calculator</a>
              <a href="/countries/pakistan/income-tax/income-tax-calculator" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">Pakistan Income Tax Calculator</a>
              <a href="/countries/pakistan" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">More Pakistan Calculators</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Related Articles</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
              <a href="/blogs/pakistan-capital-gain-tax-guide" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">Pakistan Capital Gain Tax Guide</a>
              <a href="/blogs/pakistan-income-tax-guide" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">Pakistan Income Tax Guide</a>
              <a href="/blogs/pakistan-token-tax-guide" class="block rounded border p-4 hover:border-primary transition">Pakistan Token Tax Guide</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Interesting Facts</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li>Annual property tax (UIPT) is a provincial levy, separate from federal taxes, and is charged on the Annual Rental Value of urban property.</li>
            <li>Punjab charges UIPT at 5% of the Annual Rental Value, while Sindh's headline 25% rate results in lower actual payments due to conservative valuation tables.</li>
            <li>For properties acquired on or after July 1, 2024, CGT is a flat 15% for ATL filers regardless of holding period, replacing the previous tiered system.</li>
            <li>Withholding tax under Section 236K is imposed on the buyer at the time of property purchase, with filers paying 2% to 4.5% depending on property value.</li>
            <li>Punjab and Islamabad offer approximately a 5% rebate when the full year's property tax is paid on or before September 30.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Quick Quiz</h2>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
            <p class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary">1. Which Pakistani province charges UIPT at 5% of the Annual Rental Value?</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
              <li>A) Sindh</li>
              <li>B) KPK</li>
              <li>C) Punjab</li>
              <li>D) Islamabad</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
            <p class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary">2. What is the flat CGT rate for properties acquired on or after July 1, 2024, for ATL filers?</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
              <li>A) 10%</li>
              <li>B) 12.5%</li>
              <li>C) 15%</li>
              <li>D) 17.5%</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
            <p class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. What is the maximum early-payment rebate Punjab offers on annual property tax?</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
              <li>A) 2%</li>
              <li>B) 5%</li>
              <li>C) 10%</li>
              <li>D) 15%</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Further Reading</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li><a href="https://www.fbr.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Federal Board of Revenue (FBR) – Property Tax Rules</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxation_in_Pakistan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Taxation in Pakistan – Wikipedia</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://epay.punjab.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">ePay Punjab – Online Property Tax Payment</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://iris.fbr.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">FBR IRIS Portal – Property Transaction Filing</a></li>
          </ul>

        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BlogLayout>